  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Violence and Promoting Youth Participation in the Electoral Process in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone has made substantial progress towards reconciliation since the 1991-2002 civil war that killed over 50,000 people . However, poverty and unemployment continue to be persistent challenges that are often used as tools of manipulation and triggers of violence during election season  . Isolated episodes of election-related violence have been a common occurrence in the past three post-war elections . The 2018 election is expected to follow this same trend and is in-fact predicted to be more violent than previous years according to several key stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
